# Zeitlos -- the SHORT demo: about 60 seconds, for social media.
#
#   > run automate /demo/short.zds
#
# Revision 11. Captions are 3x, one line each; the narration after the
# "|" is what is SPOKEN, and is spelled for the ear: without a speech
# pack (/speech/en.spk) tts falls back to its built-in letter-to-sound
# rules, which say "timeless" as "timless" and "designed" as
# "dizzig-nd". The respellings were checked with tts's own front end
# (sw/apps/tts/tests/t2p_cli.c); docs/demo.md, "Spelling for the ear".
#
# THE RULE: speech and action never overlap -- the voice needs about
# 60% of the CPU, and anything beside it made it stutter.

reset
interruptible off
caption-size 3
caption-pos bottom
rate 190
type-speed 45
speech on
voice synth
# jfont (Japanese) must already be running: start it before the demo.

# -- 1. hello: a desktop already at work -------------------------------
# Opened before anyone speaks: launching is what would hurt the voice.
# Once open, these are idle (clock redraws once a second), so they stay
# up under the first sentences.
run cal at 24 24
run calc at 250 70
run clock at 470 30
focus calc
type 12*34
key enter
pause 400
narrate Hello. I am Zeitlos. | Hello. I am Zeitlos.
# With a speech pack this is where the recorded voice takes over;
# without one it stays synthesised (tts logs "No recorded voice").
voice recorded
narrate Computer + OS, designed together | A cum pewter and operating system, de zined tuh gheh thur.
narrate RISC-V CPU, our own GPU, one FPGA | A risk five processor, plus graphics hardware, on one FPGA.
close calc
close cal
close clock
run gpu3d at 420 24
drag 520 130 596 170 700
key space
pause 1500
close gpu3d

# -- 2. every language -------------------------------------------------
narrate 22 keyboard layouts | Twenty two keyboard layouts, from German to Japanese.
run text at 16 16
tbicon text font
type Hello from Zeitlos!
key enter
layout de
type Grüße aus Bayern!
key enter
layout ja-us
type konnichiha!
layout us
pause 900
kill text

# -- 3. reading Markdown ----------------------------------------------
# welcome.md has headings, lists and tables: rendered, paged with Space.
narrate Markdown, rendered | And read Markdown documents.
run read /docs/welcome.md at 150 16
key alt+equal
pause 1500
key space
pause 1300
key space
pause 1300
close read

# -- 4. a photograph ---------------------------------------------------
# Said first; then the picture is decoded and shown (all at once, when
# view has finished). Tune the pause to the card: the window must not
# close before the picture is up.
narrate Every photo, in one bit | Foe tows, dithered to one bit.
run view /demo/squirrel.pgm at 0 0
key alt+equal
pause 6000
close view

# -- 5. music ----------------------------------------------------------
narrate Play music | Play music.
run midi /demo/lvb11.mid at 168 120
pause 800
melody 150 e 3 e 3 e m w q n:2 - z c n m:2 - c h m q:2 - c e 3 e 3 e m w q n:3
pause 500
close midi

# -- 6. drawing --------------------------------------------------------
narrate Or paint | Or paint.
run draw at 150 16
origin draw
click 30 50
click 72 256
drag 50 170 320 225 450
click 10 50
click 24 256
drag 120 110 200 168 350
click 30 30
drag 115 110 160 72 250
drag 160 72 205 110 250
click 10 70
drag 245 18 290 60 300
origin screen
pause 600

# -- 7. timeless -------------------------------------------------------
caption github.com/machdyne/zeitlos
video amber
pause 450
video green
pause 450
video paper
pause 450
video white
say Zeitlos. Time less cum pewting.
pause 1200
caption-off
reset
end
